-- title:
--   No pole of j along the special fibre at the cusp
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$, a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c\colon X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ be a proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ morphism with $X$ integral. The data are: a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` $\subseteq\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the expansions $j(q^d)$, $d\mid N$, together with an isomorphism $e_0$ onto the generic fibre $X\times_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}}\mathbb{Q}$ compatible with the structure maps; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$; a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose place is the $q$-adic cusp `cuspInftyFull N`, and a $\mathbb{Q}$-point $y$ of the generic fibre lying over $\varepsilon_\infty$ and carried to $x_0$ by $e_0^{-1}$; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` identified with the geometric generic fibre, whose point–place bijection is equivariant for the arithmetic Galois action (`hgal`) and whose places restrict along the base-change isomorphism $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}$`modularFunctionFieldFull N`$\cong$`modularFunctionFieldBar N` to the places of $M_0$ attached to matching points (`hcompat`); for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p\in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$, a lift $\rho_A\colon\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}\to A$ of the inclusion, a curve model $M_s(A)$ over the residue field of $A$ of `modularFunctionFieldFullC`, identified with the corresponding special fibre, and (when that residue field is algebraically closed) a degree-preserving reduction map $r$ of places satisfying `IsPlaceReductionModL` and compatible with reduction of points (`hsp`). Finally let $s$ be a closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ such that the image of $x_0$ specialises to $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$, let $m>0$, and let $a,b$ lie in the stalk of $X$ at $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$, neither in the ideal generated by the germ of $p$. Under these hypotheses it is impossible that the Laurent-series readings of $a$ and $b$ — obtained by specialisation to the stalk at the image of $x_0$, the stalk map of $e_0$ followed by the first projection, passage to the function field and $M_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ — satisfy $\mathrm{read}(a)=j(q)\cdot p^{m}\cdot\mathrm{read}(b)$; the conclusion is `False`.
--
--   This is the statement that, on a smooth proper $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-model of $X_0(N)$ with $p\nmid N$, the modular invariant $j$ acquires no pole along the special fibre near the cusp section, expressed as the impossibility of a relation $a=j\,p^{m}b$ between germs prime to $p$. It is one of the two exclusion steps feeding the statement that the germ of $j$ at the cusp section is a ratio of germs prime to $p$, and is proved by transporting the relation to infinitely many Hensel-lifted closed points of the geometric special fibres and contradicting the finiteness of the poles of the reduced $j$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_false_of_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_pow_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero.lean

